;; expect: ok
;; slice 3.21b rule 2 (GPT-6's trajectory review, finding 2): a module sees the export through
;; its own `(import Init NAME)` and its imports' horizons, the farthest of them, whatever else
;; the load admitted. wide.shard imports through Bool.decide_eq_true and is loaded first;
;; small.shard imports through Int.decEq, opens Init.Bool and cites decide_eq_true — before,
;; that citation was ambiguous with Bool.decide_eq_true once any earlier file had imported it
;; (3.21's as-built), so a module's meaning depended on the load's order.
(import "wide.shard")
(import "small.shard")
(use wide)
(def m () Nat wide_marker)
